thy package-manager consistency.","evidence_ids":["cmd-42bc02bc74dd4c3b","cmd-73a38aebe2ed4e3a","cmd-1556decbe4024e6f","cmd-1f95d3cb01994c6f","cmd-28ebea0c8c5548e1","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence of snapshot creation, deliberate divergence, completed rollback, and exact content and metadata recovery. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and service, storage, metadata, and data recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently agree with those identities.","limitations":["The exactness comparison relies on metadata and hash manifests generated by the executor before the snapshot rather than an independent verifier probe.","Lifecycle snapshots provide only bounded system-wide inventories and do not independently enumerate persistent task artifacts under /srv or /var/lib.","No cluster state was shown, but the managed topology contains only the standalone node1 and no cluster service was required."]}
